how do you negotiate a great deal this  is an important question because as  entrepreneurs we don't have tons of cash  flowing out of our wallets flowing out  of our bank accounts you need to make  every dollar stretch right you got to  make every dollar you spend count  especially in the early days and part of  that comes from negotiating great deals  with your suppliers I got a great  question from one of my readers my olive  Seif who wrote in to say Evan what is  your opinion on the go shooting with  suppliers from anywhere on top of the  original offer thank you when I'm  negotiating I always look at the size of  the company if I'm working with a bigger  company I try to negotiate as much as I  can I try to get the best possible price  because at the end of the day they won't  care so much about me but when I'm  working with a smaller company if it's a  solo entrepreneur or a really small  outfit I tend not to negotiate too much  because I want to be important to their  business and I know and you should know  how important every dollar is to your  company do you like the clients who  negotiate you down to your absolute  lowest profit margin do you like those  clients probably not so why would you be  that client to other people I like my  suppliers especially the small ones to  care about me I wanted to be one of  their favorite customers and to do that  you have to pay them so that they're  gonna make a profit off of you that's  part of business I'm not gonna overpay I  don't want you ripping me off but I want  to make sure that you are profitable  from working with me now if you're a  bigger company again I'm gonna take you  for as much as you can  here's a quick example a big company  came to me and they want to do an event  with me so I had my regular right  typically for an event depending on what  it is I'll charge between 1500 and 2500  bucks and when it came down to creating  the budget they said you got to talk to  this guy who helped bring it on and I  spoke with him and he's his own business  he's that he's a small entrepreneur he's  a solo guy and I told them on the phone  listen you know what I usually charge  1500 to 2500 bucks for this but I  understand that this is now coming out  of your pocket this isn't coming out of  the big company's pockets come out of  your pocket  I'm gonna build a relationship with you  and I'm gonna do it for you for free now  I get some exposure from it  from being part of it and maybe we can  build a long-term relationship together  that might work with that bigger company  but I don't want to take that kind of  money out of an entrepreneurs pocket  doesn't feel right to me if it's a big  company I have no problem doing it but a  small entrepreneur solo guy trying to  make his mark I don't want to be pulling  out of his pocket so I made it free for  him I could have been a cheaper price I  was feeling generous whatever  it's my typical style and it's something  I would encourage you to embrace for the  smaller entrepreneurs just think about  their situation think about where you're  coming from think about the clients who  try to nickel-and-dime you all the way  and how you don't like working with  those guys so don't be that client to  other people now assuming you're working  with somebody bigger than you know the  little tiny entrepreneur how do you get  the best deal possible the key to  negotiating is thinking about everything  that's important to that person besides  price okay price is always gonna matter  everybody cares about price no matter  what it is at your sound it's always a  factor but there are always other things  that people care about besides price as  well you just have to find out what  those things are and play up to them so  people would be willing to give you a  lower price because you're so good on  all the other factors here's a quick  example I'm I'm renting an apartment I  just closed yesterday so I'm just  signing the checks today and the place  that I liked is 20 it was listed for  $2,600 a month okay in that building  other places were going for 27 $2,800 a  month so 26 sounds like a good deal  right I wanted a better deal I liked  getting the deal so I wanted to figure  out a better way to do it if you look at  what does a landlord care about besides  money that's an opportunity to build a  negotiated better deal so I managed to  get the deal for 2450 much lower than a  2,600 that they were asking and much  lower than everything else is going in  the building how did I do it here's a  few things number one think about the  landlords they want somebody who's gonna  pay right a bad tenant somebody who  doesn't pay is gonna be a nightmare for  them they'd rather have somebody pay  less  who will pay on time every month and  somebody who doesn't pay up so I gave  them my credit score my credit score is  amazed  it's off the charts it's almost as high  as you can be and so that plays in my  favorite when going after this kind of  deal right I don't take on debt when I  do I pay it off really quickly and so I  make for a great potential tenant so I  shared the full report with them you  could see everything my entire history  to see that I pay on time the second  thing is I showed that I'm a really good  tenant I showed my office  so I've owned my own office place in a  building for maybe six years and I've  taken care of it and I have great  neighbors and everybody likes having me  in the building and I talked about that  I talked about hey I've had my own place  right down the street for six years I  love being a good neighbor I take care  of the common elements and I gave that  phone number and name of my next-door  neighbor as a reference so you can call  him up like she's known me for six years  you can talked about me being a good  neighbor and again this is something  that landlords care about they don't  want somebody coming in who's gonna be a  bad neighbor and cause problems for them  this is supposed to be a hands-off  passive income thing for them they don't  want problems so show you're not gonna  create problems I talked about my house  that I used to have how I built it up  how I sold it how I loved modern design  how I had video companies come in movie  companies come in photographers come in  and shoot the place it was featured in  magazines commercials movies and I  talked about how I look after my place  right I keep it in great condition I  looked after everything in the place and  I will treat your place like it was my  own as well and again another big  concern that landlords care about  finally on the money side I offered  instead of first and last month's rent  I offered six months rent in advance so  I'm paying less but in pain more upfront  I had the cash on hand so I decided to  go for it and again it makes it an  easier decision for the landlord so I  got a great price better than anything  else in the building but I paid more  upfront I showed that I have a great  credit score I'm gonna pay I showed that  I'm a great neighbor and I showed that I  care about the place that I live in and  I'm gonna take care of it so these are  all things that they're gonna care about  beyond just a price so think about any  deal you're negotiating with any  supplier I think about everything that  they  here about beyond just a price whatever  can work in your favor  to show how great a potential customer  you can be for them so that they'll be  willing to give you a discounted price  if you do it it's a great way to build  an amazing relationship with your  suppliers and also save you a lot of  money believe those you're watching like  the video please give it a thumbs up  below it always makes me want to do more  for you and I'd love to hear what you  have to think how do you negotiate with  your suppliers leave a comment below let  me know and if you have a question leave  in a comment section below I'll make a  video response thank you so much and  I'll see y